This program provides Typst support in FlashTeX. It is not an official Typst
product and is not endorsed by the Typst project.

It links, unmodified, the Typst compiler crates version 0.15.1 (typst,
typst-layout, typst-pdf, typst-kit and the crates they depend on) from the
Typst project, https://github.com/typst/typst, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. No Typst file is modified (Apache-2.0 §4(b)): the crates
are used exactly as published on crates.io, pinned by version and checksum in
Cargo.lock, with no [patch] and no fork.

Apache-2.0 §4(a) and §4(d): the licence texts of every linked crate and the
NOTICE files of the Apache-2.0 components -- typst/typst's own NOTICE (pinned
by SHA-256), typst-assets, hayagriva, citationberg and subsetter -- are
reproduced in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, which
licenses/third_party.py generates from Cargo.lock for every distributed build
and which ship with it (DESIGN.md §15.8). That script fails the build on an
unknown licence, a missing licence text or a missing NOTICE.

No font is compiled into this program (it is built without typst-kit's
`embedded-fonts`); fonts are separate files that carry their own licences.

It never links, calls or copies code from crates/flashtex-engine (GPL-2.0-or-
later); scripts/check-license-boundary.sh (check D) enforces that.
